    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **62 run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (which handles `POST /api/owners`), satisfying the spec and the new `Cp50Tests`.\n\nSince the `addOwner` signature is fixed by the generated `OwnersApi` interface, I read the header with the standard Spring `RequestContextHolder` idiom rather than adding a parameter. Changes:\n\n- **Store** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`): a static `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> IDEMPOTENCY_KEYS` mapping each seen `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 the id of the owner originally created for it.\n- **Early short-circuit** at the top of `addOwner`: if the request carries an `Idempotency-Key` already in the map, it looks up that owner and returns it with **200 OK** \u2014 before the identity/household duplicate rules that would otherwise reject the repeat with 409.\n- **Record on create**: after a successful `saveOwner`, the key is stored against the new owner's id.\n- **`currentIdempotencyKey()` helper**: reads the `Idempotency-Key` header off the active request, returning `null` when absent/blank or when there's no servlet request \u2014 so requests without the header behave exactly as before.\n\nThe behavior: first create with a key returns 201 (created); a repeat with the same key returns the original owner with 200, no duplicate created.",
