    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, traced through `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (which implements the generated `OwnersApi`), the `ClinicService` facade, and the JPA repository.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Framework gate (before the method body)\n\n1. **Authentication** (if `petclinic.security.enable=true`): HTTP Basic auth required (`anyRequest().authenticated()`).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`) \u2014 on failure, short-circuits to **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Constraints checked:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-separated parts)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (like firstName, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)` (note: **no** E.164 pattern here \u2014 that's enforced later, imperatively)\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`; `address`/`addressLine1` \u2014 non-blank `@Pattern` + `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (optional)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)` (optional)\n3. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (enforced only when security is enabled; the disable-security profile does not turn on method security).\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Idempotency short-circuit (side-effect: read cache)\n\n4. Read `Idempotency-Key` header. If it maps to a previously created owner in the static in-memory `IDEMPOTENCY_KEYS` map, **return that existing owner with 200 OK** \u2014 no new owner created.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Map & normalize (mutations on the entity)\n\n5. MapStruct `toOwner(dto)` \u2192 new `Owner` (ignores `id` and `pets`).\n6. `applyAddress(owner)` \u2014 normalize/compose address fields.\n7. **Normalize telephone** to E.164 via `normalizeTelephone()`, which also validates national-number length (`NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS`) \u2014 can reject.\n8. **Normalize email** \u2014 lower-cased.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Imperative validations (throw 400/409/429)\n\n9. `validateEmailDomain(email)` \u2014 rejects disposable domains (`DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS`).\n10. `validatePostcode(postcode, city)` \u2014 region/postcode-range consistency (`REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES`).\n11. **Registration date not in the future** \u2014 if `registrationDate > server date` \u2192 **400**.\n12. Roll `registrationDate` to a business day (`toBusinessDay`: skips weekends + hard-coded 2026 `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS`) and **set it on the owner**.\n13. **Per-day cap** \u2014 count owners already registered for that business date; if `\u2265 100` \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n14. **Set `bulkSignupWarning = (createdToday > 80)`**.\n15. Compute & **set `householdId`** (from normalized last name + postcode).\n16. **Identity-duplicate check** \u2014 if any non-deleted owner shares `identityKey` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n17. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 if the household already has a non-deleted member and the request did not set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n18. **Per-city cap** \u2014 if that city already has `\u2265 50` owners \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Derived fields set before save\n\n19. **Set** `namesakeCount`, `householdSize` (household members + 1), `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`.\n20. **Set `customerCode`** \u2014 SHA-256-derived from city/postcode/telephone/lastName, then de-duplicated.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Persistence & external effects\n\n21. **DB insert** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` inside a `@Transactional` boundary; `id` assigned by `GenerationType.IDENTITY`.\n22. **Mutate idempotency cache** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was present, store `key \u2192 owner.getId()` in the static `IDEMPOTENCY_KEYS` map.\n23. **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: ...\")` (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n24. **Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 CREATED** with the mapped `OwnerDto` (whose membership/locality/fiscal fields are computed purely during mapping).\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n- **All owner business logic lives in the controller**, not the service \u2014 `saveOwner` is a thin transactional pass-through to `ownerRepository.save`.\n- The entity `Owner` carries its own constraints (`@NotEmpty` address/city/telephone/first/last, E.164 `@Pattern`, `@Email`), but these only fire if Hibernate validate-on-persist is active; the request-time enforcement is the DTO's plus the imperative checks above.\n- **No** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.), entity listeners, auditing, event publishing, password encoding, or email/notification sending occur in this path \u2014 `validateEmailDomain` only validates, it does not send anything."
